course: dictionary
lesson: 994
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Bogey is a good example: it can mean a bit of dried snot, a golf score, an imaginary monster, or something you fear. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. The words around it are the clues.
explain: «A bogey is dried mucus around trapped dust; picking spreads germs to your fingers and on to others and can make the nose bleed.» Here the sentence is about the body, so bogey means a bit of dried snot. Picking your nose is not a good idea, because it spreads germs.
explain: Always ask: what is the topic? A golf course means a golf score. A bedtime story about a monster means the bogeyman. When you know the topic, pick the meaning that fits and then check it by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A bogey can mean a bit of dried mucus (snot) from inside your nose. Americans say «booger».
fact: In golf, a bogey is a score of one more than par on a hole.
fact: A bogeyman is an imaginary evil spirit or monster used to scare children.
fact: «Bogey» can also mean something people fear or worry about, as in «Maths is my bogey subject».
fact: In Australia, slang «bogey» can mean a swim or a bath.
exercise: On the golf course, Dad says, «I got a bogey on the sixth hole.» What does bogey mean here? | A monster that scares children | Something you fear | A bit of dried snot | *One more shot than par on a hole
exercise: Lily says, «The bogeyman will get you if you don't go to sleep!» What is a bogeyman? | *An imaginary monster used to scare children | A real golfer who is very good | A swim or a bath | A bit of dried mucus
exercise: Nadia says, «Maths is my bogey subject.» What does bogey mean in this sentence? | A bit of dried snot | *Something you fear or worry about | A very fast car | A score in golf
test: «A bogey is dried mucus around trapped dust; picking spreads germs to your fingers and on to others.» According to the text, what can picking your nose do? | *Spread germs and can make the nose bleed | Cure a cold | Make you taller | Stop bogeys forming
test: Sam says, «I'm going for a bogey before tea, mate.» Sam is Australian. What does bogey mean? | *A swim or a bath | A golf score | A bit of dried snot | An imaginary monster
exam: Which meaning of bogey is used in «A bogey is dried mucus around trapped dust»? | An imaginary monster used to scare children | A golf score of one more than par | Something people fear or worry about | *A bit of dried snot from your nose
